.TH NOSTR-HOME-FETCH 1 "2026-09-25" "nostr-homed 0.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nostr-home-fetch \- unprivileged portable-home fetch helper (broker + provisioner spawn)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nostr-home-fetch
(\fB\-\-staging\-fd\fR \fIN\fR | \fB\-\-staging\-dir\fR \fIPATH\fR)
[\fB\-\-allow\-insecure\fR]
.PP
Control JSON is read from stdin (max 16 KiB).
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nostr-home-fetch
is the single-purpose helper binary that materializes a portable-home tree
(pointer + manifest + chunks) into a staging directory. It is designed to
be exec'd by a parent process (the broker
.BR nostr-authd (8),
or
.BR nostr-homed-provision-pull (1))
after privileges have been dropped to a dedicated unprivileged uid.
.PP
The helper never reads from /run/nostr-auth or the account file itself \(em
the caller passes the pubkey, home_key, relay list and Blossom list as a
control-JSON blob on stdin. All Blossom hosts are subject to the SSRF gate:
private ranges (RFC 1918, link-local, ULA, loopback) and non-https:// URLs
are rejected unless
.B \-\-allow\-insecure
is set.
.PP
The helper refuses to run as root. This is deliberate \(em the entire
security model assumes an unprivileged process. Callers must fork, drop, then
exec.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-staging\-fd \fIN\fR
Write materialized files below the open directory file descriptor N (passed
via
.BR fdopendir (3)-compatible
inheritance). Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-staging\-dir .
.TP
.B \-\-staging\-dir \fIPATH\fR
Write materialized files below PATH. The helper creates PATH if it does not
exist. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-staging\-fd .
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-insecure
Skip the SSRF gate on Blossom hosts. For interop tests only.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT CODES
.RS
.TP 4
.B 0
Success. Staging directory is populated.
.TP 4
.B 64
Bad argument (missing staging target; both targets; refuse-to-run-as-root).
.TP 4
.B 65
SSRF gate rejected a Blossom host or scheme.
.TP 4
.B 71
Network failure (relay unreachable, Blossom 5xx, DNS).
.TP 4
.B 72
Manifest decode failure.
.TP 4
.B 73
Size cap exceeded (chunk or manifest larger than the compiled ceiling).
.TP 4
.B 74
Timeout budget exceeded.
.TP 4
.B 75
Decrypt failure.
.TP 4
.B 76
Internal error (I/O, allocator, unexpected state).
.RE
.SH CONTROL JSON
The helper reads a JSON object from stdin (bounded at 16 KiB). Required
keys: pubkey (64-hex), home_key (64-hex), relays (array of wss:// URLs),
blossom (array of https:// URLs). Optional keys: relay_timeout_ms,
chunk_size_max, allow_insecure (bool). See the source of
.I porthome_fetch_ctl.h
for the exhaustive schema.
.SH STDOUT / STDERR
Stdout is detached before any network I/O: the helper saves the caller's
original stdout as a private progress channel and redirects the shared
stdout to /dev/null. This prevents stray printf calls from libnostr or
libcurl from corrupting the parent broker's progress lexer. Human-readable
diagnostics go to stderr; the progress channel emits structured NDJSON.
.SH SECURITY
Refuses to run as root or euid 0. Enforces a per-fetch total-time budget.
Bounds all remote size reads. Wipes the home_key from memory before exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nostr-homed-provision-pull (1),
.BR nostr-home-syncd (8)
